# Owner: devops-engineer (P1-F02-T08, cache rules added P2-F04-T08). Cloudflare Pages `_headers`
# for the client project (keep-walking-preview). This is Phase 1/2's only "preview" environment
# (docs/tech/environments.md section 1: no production exists yet) -- keep it out of search indexes
# (TL-N07) since it is a spike build, not the real game.
#
# Most of the Vite build output (index.html, hashed JS/CSS filenames) needs no override here:
# Cloudflare Pages already serves it correctly and cache-busts by filename. The `/kw/*` rules below
# are for the asset pipeline's own output (tools/art/out/client/, copied into `dist/kw/` by
# apps/client's build, docs/tech/asset-delivery.md section 6.1) -- those filenames are NOT
# content-hashed by Vite, so they need explicit cache headers per asset-delivery.md section 6.2.
# Tile-specific rules live in infra/pages/keep-walking-map/_headers (separate project, tech note
# F02 section 7.5) -- this file never repeats those.
#
# Checked with infra/scripts/lint-headers.sh (infra/scripts/test/test-lint-headers.sh) after every
# edit: none of the `/kw/*` rules below overlap on the same header name for any representative path
# (the broad `/kw/fonts/*` cache rule and the two specific `/kw/fonts/*.woff2` / `*.ttf`
# content-type rules set DIFFERENT header names on the same file, which is not an overlap -- only
# two rules setting the SAME header name for the SAME path is the P1-X41 bug this lint catches).

/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Version pointer (asset-pipeline 5, asset-delivery.md 6.2): must revalidate on every load so a
# new build's manifest is never served stale from a client's HTTP cache. Cloudflare Pages already
# sends a strong ETag for every static file it serves, so `no-cache` (revalidate-before-use, not
# "don't cache") plus that automatic ETag together give a 304 on an unchanged manifest -- no ETag
# directive is set explicitly here, there is no way to set one in `_headers` and none is needed.
/kw/asset-manifest.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Art, fonts, audio the pipeline stages: immutable for a year. Every art/audio file's own URL
# already embeds `?v=<sha256 8 chars>` (asset-manifest.json `files[].url`, asset-delivery.md
# section 5) so a changed file is always a new URL -- there is nothing to invalidate.
/kw/art/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/kw/audio/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Fonts: same immutable cache as above, plus the two content types Cloudflare Pages does not infer
# correctly on its own for these two extensions (asset-delivery.md section 6.2, section 7 font
# table). This rule and the two below it set different header names on the same file (Cache-Control
# here, Content-Type below) -- not an overlap, see file header comment.
/kw/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/kw/fonts/*.woff2
  Content-Type: font/woff2

/kw/fonts/*.ttf
  Content-Type: font/ttf
